## Route builds through the configured Lakehouse transport

Context: Knowledge Graph builds using a Lakebase graph backend selected the
general SQL warehouse and created their source client with the default Thrift
transport. Lakehouse/RT warehouses reject Thrift even when Settings already
stored a Lakehouse warehouse with Statement Execution API enabled.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/helpers/DatabricksHelpers.py
   Route every triple-store build through the configured Lakehouse warehouse,
   with the existing global SQL warehouse fallback.
2. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/_build_pipeline.py
   Propagate the persisted Lakehouse Statement Execution API setting to the
   SQL client used for source VIEW creation and build queries.
3. tests/units/settings/test_delta_warehouse_config.py
   Added regression coverage for Lakebase builds selecting the Lakehouse
   warehouse.
4. tests/back/core/digitaltwin/test_build_pipeline_units.py
   Added regression coverage for forwarding the configured SQL transport to
   the build client.
5. src/mcp-server/app.yaml
   Regenerated the deployed MCP runtime configuration for the 09x UI and
   Lakebase registry resources.
6. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaTripleStoreBuildPipeline.py
   Propagated the Lakehouse Statement Execution API setting through the
   Databricks-only Build endpoint pipeline.
7. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_build_pipeline.py
   Added regression coverage for the transport used by the Build button's
   specialized Delta pipeline.

